---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Layout
	title="Median & Empirical Relationship | Statistics | Class 10 | The Concepts Adda"
	description="Learn how to find Median of grouped data using cumulative frequency and master the empirical relationship 3 Median = Mode + 2 Mean for Class 10 NCERT Mathematics."
>
	<main class="lesson-page">
		<div class="lesson-container">
			<a href="/statistics" class="back-link">
				<span class="back-arrow">←</span>
				<span>Back to Statistics</span>
			</a>

			<!-- LESSON HEADER -->
			<section class="lesson-header">
				<div class="lesson-number">03</div>
				<div class="lesson-header-copy">
					<div class="lesson-label">LESSON 03 · CLASS 10 MATHEMATICS (NCERT)</div>
					<h1>Median & <span>Empirical Relationship</span></h1>
					<p>
						Master cumulative frequency tables, Median formula calculation, and applying the empirical rule (3 Median = Mode + 2 Mean).
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTENT LAYOUT -->
			<section class="content-layout">
				<article class="lesson-content">

					<!-- 01 · MEDIAN CLASS & CF -->
					<div class="topic-label">01 · MEDIAN CLASS</div>
					<h2>Cumulative Frequency & Median Class</h2>
					<p>
						To find the median of grouped data, construct the <strong>cumulative frequency (cf)</strong> column. Find $N = \sum f_i$. The <strong>Median Class</strong> is the class interval whose cumulative frequency is just greater than (or equal to) <strong>N / 2</strong>.
					</p>

					<!-- 02 · MEDIAN FORMULA -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">02 · MEDIAN FORMULA</div>
					<h2>Median Formula for Grouped Data</h2>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>Median = l + [ ( (N/2) - cf ) / f ] × h</strong>
					</div>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>l</span>
							<p>Lower limit of median class.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>N</span>
							<p>Number of observations (N = Σfᵢ).</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>cf</span>
							<p>Cumulative frequency of class <strong>preceding</strong> the median class.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>f</span>
							<p>Frequency of the median class.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>h</span>
							<p>Class size (assuming equal class sizes).</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 03 · EMPIRICAL RELATIONSHIP -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">03 · EMPIRICAL RULE</div>
					<h2>Empirical Relationship Between Measures of Central Tendency</h2>

					<div class="formula-box">
						<strong>3 × Median = Mode + 2 × Mean</strong>
					</div>

					<!-- 04 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLE -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">04 · SOLVED NCERT EXAMPLE</div>
					<h2>Step-by-Step Problem Solving</h2>

					<div class="example-card">
						<div class="example-header">
							<span class="example-badge">EXAMPLE 1</span>
							<h3>A survey regarding heights (in cm) of 51 girls of Class X was conducted. Find the median height.</h3>
						</div>
						<div class="example-solution">
							<div class="calc-box">
								Class Interval &nbsp;|&nbsp; Frequency fᵢ &nbsp;|&nbsp; Cumulative Frequency cf<br/>
								135 - 140 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 4 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 4<br/>
								140 - 145 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 7 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 11 &nbsp;(cf of preceding class!)<br/>
								145 - 150 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 18 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 29 &nbsp;◄ MEDIAN CLASS (cf ≥ 25.5)<br/>
								150 - 155 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 11 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 40<br/>
								155 - 160 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 6 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 46<br/>
								160 - 165 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 5 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp; 51 (N = 51)
							</div>

							<p style="margin-top:14px;"><strong>Identifying Parameters</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								N = 51 ⟹ N/2 = 25.5<br/>
								Median Class = 145 - 150<br/>
								Lower Limit l = 145, Class Size h = 5<br/>
								f = 18 (median class frequency)<br/>
								cf = 11 (preceding cumulative frequency)
							</div>

							<p style="margin-top:14px;"><strong>Calculating Median</strong>:</p>
							<div class="calc-box">
								Median = 145 + [ (25.5 - 11) / 18 ] × 5<br/>
								Median = 145 + [ 14.5 / 18 ] × 5 = 145 + (72.5 / 18) = 145 + 4.03 = <strong>149.03 cm</strong>
							</div>
							<p style="margin-top:10px;">Median height of girls is <strong>149.03 cm</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- 05 · QUICK SUMMARY -->
					<div class="topic-label second-label">05 · QUICK SUMMARY</div>
					<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>

					<div class="summary-list">
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>01</span>
							<p>Median class is chosen where cumulative frequency <strong>cf ≥ N/2</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>02</span>
							<p>Median formula: <strong>Median = l + [ ( (N/2) - cf ) / f ] × h</strong>.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="summary-item">
							<span>03</span>
							<p>Empirical relationship formula: <strong>3 Median = Mode + 2 Mean</strong>.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- LESSON NAVIGATION -->
					<div class="lesson-navigation">
						<a href="/statistics/mode-of-grouped-data" class="previous-lesson">
							<span>←</span>
							<div>
								<small>PREVIOUS LESSON</small>
								<strong>Mode of Grouped Data</strong>
							</div>
						</a>

						<a href="/statistics/pyqs" class="next-lesson">
							<div>
								<small>NEXT LESSON</small>
								<strong>Previous Year PYQs</strong>
							</div>
							<span>→</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</article>

				<!-- SIDEBAR -->
				<aside class="lesson-sidebar">
					<div class="sidebar-card">
						<div class="sidebar-title">STATISTICS</div>
						<div class="progress-text">Lesson 03 of 04</div>
						<div class="progress-bar">
